SEG = "FLD"
CAT = "fnswField"
Q = [
    ("Under s 6B, an unlicensed person may use a firearm on an approved safety course while supervised by:",
     "An approved firearms instructor", ["Any licensed friend", "A uniformed police officer", "A club secretary"],
     "Section 6B(1)(b) exempts a person taking part in an approved firearms safety training course while under the supervision of a firearms instructor approved by the Commissioner."),
    ("When carrying a firearm around a range, the NSW Police users guide says to point the muzzle safely and keep:",
     "The action open", ["The magazine fitted", "The safety off", "The bolt closed"],
     "The users guide says that if you are carrying a firearm at a range you must point the muzzle in a safe direction and keep the action open."),
    ("Before shooting at a range, the NSW Police users guide says you must check:",
     "That range's own rules", ["The weather forecast", "Your licence expiry", "The club's accounts"],
     "The users guide gives general range rules but says you must check the specific rules of the range before shooting there."),
    ("The NSW Police users guide says shooting ranges also include moveable ranges, such as:",
     "Air gun stalls at fairs", ["Paddocks used once a year", "A backyard with a mound", "Any vacant rural block"],
     "The users guide says shooting ranges may be indoors or outdoors and include moveable ranges, such as the air gun shooting ranges found at carnivals or fairs."),
    ("According to the NSW Police users guide, who is responsible for safety at a range?",
     "Every person there", ["Only the range officer", "Only the club committee", "Only those firing"],
     "The users guide's range rules say every person at a range is responsible for safety, not just the range officer."),
    ("The users guide says the maximum distance your firearm can shoot depends on the firearm, the ammunition and:",
     "Conditions such as wind", ["The time of day", "The colour of the target", "The shooter's age"],
     "The users guide says the maximum range depends on the firearm and its ammunition, and environmental factors such as wind can change the projectile's velocity and trajectory."),
    ("Why does the users guide say to take extra care over what lies beyond a clay target or an animal?",
     "Nothing may stop the shot", ["It slows the projectile", "It stops all ricochets", "It shortens the range"],
     "The users guide says moving objects such as clay targets or animals may not have anything behind them to stop the projectile, so you must know where it will go if you hit or miss."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code says to check your firing zone with special care when shooting at:",
     "Birds in flight", ["Paper targets", "Steel gongs", "Rabbits on a bank"],
     "The Code says to check your firing zone with special care when shooting at birds in flight, because the shot can travel well beyond the target."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code gives the effective danger range of a .303 as about:",
     "3.6 km", ["1.5 km", "2.4 km", "5.5 km"],
     "The Code's table gives about 3600 metres for a .303, compared with about 1.5 km for a .22 rimfire and about 4 km for a .308."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code gives the effective danger range of a shotgun firing BB shot as about:",
     "450 m", ["150 m", "250 m", "1.5 km"],
     "The Code's table gives about 450 metres for BB shot, compared with about 250 metres for number 6 shot."),
    ("Why does the Code say rimfire and centrefire bullets are prone to ricochet far from the shooter?",
     "They slow near the end", ["They spin too fast", "They are very light in weight", "They break apart"],
     "The Code says rimfire and centrefire projectiles are prone to ricochet as they lose velocity at the end of their travel, which can be a considerable distance away."),
    ("The blind zone just past the muzzle that you cannot see through a telescopic sight varies with:",
     "The sight's power", ["The rifle's calibre", "The time of day", "The target's size"],
     "The Code says there is a danger zone at the muzzle and a short distance beyond that a telescopic sight does not show, and its size varies with the power of the sight."),
    ("When adjusting open sights, the Code's rule is front sight follows and rear sight:",
     "Moves in reverse", ["Follows it too", "Stays fixed", "Moves up and down only"],
     "The Code's sighting-in rule for open sights is 'front sight follows, rear sight reverse'. With a telescopic sight you follow the arrows."),
    ("After zeroing at the Code's first firing point, you should next fire at a target from:",
     "100 metres", ["50 metres", "200 metres", "300 metres"],
     "The Code suggests a first firing point at 25 m, adjusting until point of aim and point of entry match, then firing from 100 metres and adjusting again."),
    ("When sighting in with a telescopic sight, the Code says to adjust it by:",
     "Following its arrows", ["Reversing its arrows", "Tapping the tube", "Moving the mounts"],
     "The Code says that with a telescopic sight you follow the arrows on the adjustment turrets, while open sights use 'front sight follows, rear sight reverse'."),
    ("When zeroing on an established outdoor range, the Code says to make sure:",
     "Livestock are out of danger", ["The wind is calm", "The sun is behind the shooter", "The target is new"],
     "The Code says to ensure that both livestock and personal property are in no danger and that people nearby are aware of what you are doing."),
    ("In the field, if you drop your firearm, the Code says you should:",
     "Check for a blocked barrel", ["Fire a test shot straight away", "Tighten the scope mounts", "Clean the action"],
     "The Code says to check the barrel for obstructions immediately after dropping a firearm, and always to unload it before checking."),
    ("The NSW Police users guide says that under the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals Act 1979, a hunter must not:",
     "Inflict unnecessary pain", ["Hunt after sunset on any land", "Use a scope", "Shoot feral species"],
     "The users guide reminds hunters and pest controllers that the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals Act 1979 forbids inflicting unnecessary pain on an animal while hunting, shooting or trapping it."),
    ("The NSW Police users guide describes a duty of care as a legal obligation to:",
     "Avoid harming other people", ["Report every shot fired", "Insure every firearm", "Shoot only on weekends"],
     "The users guide says a duty of care requires a person to exercise a reasonable standard of care where it is reasonably foreseeable that an act may harm another person."),
    ("Someone is badly hurt in a firearm accident and needs urgent medical attention. The users guide says to:",
     "Call an ambulance", ["Drive to the clubhouse", "Phone the Registry", "Write a report first"],
     "The users guide says that if there is a serious firearms accident or injury and the person requires urgent medical attention, call an ambulance."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code says people involved with firearms should act as:",
     "Ambassadors in the community", ["Volunteer police officers", "Club membership recruiters", "Informal range inspectors"],
     "Principle 11's explanation says those involved with firearms should be ambassadors in the community for current and prospective firearm owners and users."),
    ("According to the NSW Police users guide, a range officer's role is to:",
     "Supervise the range", ["Sell ammunition to shooters", "Issue licences", "Repair firearms"],
     "The users guide says a range officer holds a supervisory role at the range, and you must obey the officer's commands and directions to keep everyone safe."),
    ("Under s 6B of the Firearms Act, an unlicensed visitor may shoot at an approved range while a licensed person supervises:",
     "Only that one person", ["Up to five people", "From the clubhouse", "Any number of guests"],
     "Section 6B(1A) requires direct supervision, so the supervisor supervises one person only. The exemption also does not cover prohibited firearms."),
    ("The s 6B exemption for unlicensed shooters on approved ranges does not apply to anyone under the age of:",
     "12", ["10", "14", "16"],
     "Section 6B(3) says the exemption for unlicensed persons at approved ranges and on approved safety courses does not apply to a person under 12 years of age."),
]
